      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-8{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=3{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}+6{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-(-4{b}_{2})+2(3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-8{b}_{2})+2(3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
